      "writtenOn": "2014-02-21T00:07:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was answered in PS 13. Its actually done as a hack but as per your suggestion, now it seems like a good candidate for abstract class. I will make that change in next patch.\n\nReply in PS 13 was...\n\nAs this is optional backend so any pymongo related imports need to be differed till its used. So no module level imports.\n\nIdeally I would have done following\n\u003ccode\u003e\nfrom pymongo import son_manipulator\nclass BaseTransform(son_manipulator.SONManipulator)\n\u003c/code\u003e\n\nNow added this, to circumvent related mongo logic. Without this, it complains at following logic https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-python-driver/blob/master/pymongo/database.py#L96",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAUX/+e/0\u003d",
      "revId": "220bb151fa90409751879267bd5c5647ef780f43",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
