        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-02-20T23:11:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a case where the SON transform wouldn\u0027t need the work from BaseTransform?  Your docstring indicates that since dogpile.cache stores things as a special object, this logic is needed.  Wouldn\u0027t that imply this is _always_ needed?  If so, does it make sense to make this logic always occur?  This will always be used in the context of dogpile.cache and the SON manipulator (user specified) might need to be layered after the part that strips out the CachedValue object",
      "revId": "220bb151fa90409751879267bd5c5647ef780f43",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAUX/+eUY\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/cache/backends/mongo.py",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 477,
      "author": {
        "id": 1091
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-02-21T00:07:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes..this is always needed, that\u0027s why BaseTransform is used if no custom SON manipulator is specified.\n\nI think if the custom class is need to be stored, then custom manipulator can do complete transformation instead of doing it in layers as it can be confusing. Also have not seen if layering approach even works.\n\nI have provided reply around similar concern in PS13 around this.\n\nI have seen a situation where dogpile caching decorator is applied where a custom object is returned instead of a simple dictionary or array. In that case, the person will need to have custom encoding and decoding logic while saving to and reading from mongo if there is need to have automatic conversion from mongo dict data to class.\nPlease see following for further details. http://api.mongodb.org/python/current/examples/custom_type.html#automatic-encoding-and-decoding",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAUX/+e/U\u003d",
      "revId": "220bb151fa90409751879267bd5c5647ef780f43",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
